Removing all type imports from 'ajv' does exactly that. It also fixes the RUNTIME risk: if CI's runtime loaded ajv 6, `new Ajv({strict: false, validateFormats: false})` — ajv 6 ignores unknown options silently (no strict option validation), and `validateFormats` absent → formats only validated when registered. Our schemas don't use `format`, so runtime behavior would coincide. But the unit tests on CI would then run against ajv 6 — behavior compatible for the features we use (draft-07 required/type/enum, errorsText). Fine either way.

